cript><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-message kadence-blocks-form-warning\">Please enable JavaScript in your browser to submit the form</div><style>.kadence-form-7744_eacc90-ec .kadence-blocks-form-field.kb-submit-field { display: none; }</style></noscript></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<style>.kb-table-of-content-nav.kb-table-of-content-id197838_d9cd68-43 .kb-table-of-content-wrap{padding-top:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);padding-right:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);padding-bottom:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);padding-left:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);}.kb-table-of-content-nav.kb-table-of-content-id197838_d9cd68-43 .kb-table-of-contents-title-wrap{padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.kb-table-of-content-nav.kb-table-of-content-id197838_d9cd68-43 .kb-table-of-contents-title{font-weight:regular;font-style:normal;}.kb-table-of-content-nav.kb-table-of-content-id197838_d9cd68-43 .kb-table-of-content-wrap .kb-table-of-content-list{font-weight:regular;font-style:normal;margin-top:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;}</style>\n\n\n<p>Are you a resident of Clackamas County and need to understand how the county&#8217;s court system works? In this article, we&#8217;ll provide you with a detailed overview of the Clackamas County Circuit Court. We&#8217;ll discuss the court&#8217;s jurisdiction, its structure, the types of cases it handles, and much more. Let&#8217;s dive in!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is the Clackamas County Circuit Court?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court is a trial court located in Oregon&#8217;s Clackamas County. It is one of the 27 circuit courts in the state of Oregon and has jurisdiction over all civil and criminal cases that occur within Clackamas County. The court is responsible for interpreting and enforcing the law within its jurisdiction.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Jurisdiction of the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court has jurisdiction over all civil and criminal cases that occur within Clackamas County. Civil cases are disputes between individuals or organizations, such as lawsuits over contract disputes or personal injury claims. Criminal cases involve the violation of state law and include crimes such as theft, assault, and drug offenses. The Clackamas County Circuit Court also handles juvenile cases and domestic relations cases such as divorce, child custody, and child support.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>see also Albany County Criminal Court</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Structure of the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court is divided into several divisions, including the civil division, criminal division, family law division, and juvenile division. Each division is responsible for handling specific types of cases. The court also has a small claims division for cases involving claims of $10,000 or less.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Judges of the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court is presided over by elected judges who serve six-year terms. The number of judges serving on the court varies based on the workload of the court. Each judge is responsible for hearing cases within their assigned division and making decisions based on the evidence presented in court.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Types of Cases Heard in the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court hears a wide variety of cases, including:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Civil cases, such as contract disputes and personal injury claims</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Criminal cases, such as theft, assault, and drug offenses</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Juvenile cases, such as delinquency and dependency cases</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Domestic relations cases, such as divorce, child custody, and child support</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Small claims cases involving claims of $10,000 or less</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Filing a Case in the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>To file a case in the Clackamas County Circuit Court, you must first determine which division your case falls under. Once you have determined the appropriate division, you can obtain the necessary forms from the court&#8217;s website or by visiting the court in person. You must then complete the forms and file them with the court along with the appropriate filing fees.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Appearing in the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are required to appear in the Clackamas County Circuit Court, it is important to dress appropriately and arrive on time. You should bring all necessary documents and any evidence related to your case. Failure to appear in court can result in a warrant for your arrest, so it&#8217;s essential to take your court appearances seriously.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Court Records in the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Court records in the Clackamas County Circuit Court are available to the public, although certain types of information may be restricted due to privacy concerns. You can access court records online through the Oregon Judicial Information Network (OJIN) or by visiting the court in person. There may be fees associated with obtaining copies of court records.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Legal Resources in the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court provides a variety of legal resources to the public, including self-help centers, legal aid services, and mediation programs. These resources can help you navigate the court system and understand your legal rights.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Jury Duty in the Clackamas County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are a resident of Clackamas County, you may be called for jury duty in the Clackamas County Circuit Court. Jury duty is an important civic responsibility and helps ensure that individuals receive a fair trial. If you are selected for jury duty, you will receive a summons in the mail and will be required to appear in court on the specified date.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Circuit Court Case Search</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you need to search for a case in the Clackamas County Circuit Court, you can do so online through the Oregon Judicial Information Network (OJIN) or by visiting the court in person. You may need to provide certain information, such as the case number or the names of the parties involved, to access the case information.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Court Case Lookup</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Court Case Lookup allows you to search for cases in the Clackamas County Circuit Court online. You can search by case number, party name, or attorney name. The case lookup may also provide information about upcoming court dates and the status of the case.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Circuit Court Judges</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court has several judges who preside over cases in the court. The judges are responsible for interpreting and applying the law, making rulings on legal issues, and overseeing court proceedings. You can learn more about the judges and their backgrounds on the court&#8217;s website.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>see also Lynn District Court</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Circuit Court in Oregon City, OR</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court is located in Oregon City, Oregon, and serves the residents of Clackamas County. The court handles a variety of civil and criminal cases, including traffic violations, small claims, and domestic relations cases. If you need to appear in court, it&#8217;s important to arrive on time and be prepared with all the necessary documents and evidence.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Criminal Court Docket</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Criminal Court Docket provides information about upcoming criminal court cases in the Clackamas County Circuit Court. You can search for cases by date, defendant name, or case number. The docket may also provide information about the charges and court location.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Court Live Stream</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court does not currently offer live streaming of court proceedings. However, members of the public can attend court hearings in person and observe the proceedings. It&#8217;s important to dress appropriately and follow all court rules and procedures.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Court Phone Number</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court can be reached by phone at (503) 655-8447. The court&#8217;s hours of operation are Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. If you need to speak with someone about a specific case or legal issue, you may need to provide certain information to verify your identity and access the information you need.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clackamas County Divorce Records</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Divorce records in Clackamas County are available to the public, although certain information may be restricted due to privacy concerns. You can obtain divorce records by contacting the Clackamas County Circuit Court or the Oregon State Vital Records Office. There may be fees associated with obtaining copies of divorce records, and you may need to provide certain information to verify your identity and access the records.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Clackamas County Circuit Court is an essential component of the legal system in Clackamas County, Oregon. Understanding the court&#8217;s jurisdiction, structure, and procedures can help you navigate the court system and ensure that your legal rights are protected. Whether you are filing a case or appearing in court, it&#8217;s essential to take the process seriously and prepare accordingly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">FAQs</h2>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>How do I file a case in the Clackamas County Circuit Court?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>You must first determine which division your case falls under and obtain the necessary forms from the court&#8217;s website or by visiting the court in person. You must then complete the forms and file them with the court along with the appropriate filing fees.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"2\">\n<li><strong>Can I access court records online?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Yes, you can access court records online through the Oregon Judicial Information Network (OJIN) or by visiting the court in person.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>What types of cases does the Clackamas County Circuit Court hear?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The court hears civil cases, criminal cases, juvenile cases, domestic relations cases, and small claims cases involving claims of $10,000 or less.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"4\">\n<li><strong>What should I do if I am required to appear in court?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>You should dress appropriately and arrive on time. You should also bring all necessary documents and evidence related to your case.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"5\">\n<li><strong>What legal resources are available in the Clackamas County Circuit Court?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The court provides self-help centers, legal aid services, and mediation programs to help individuals navigate the court system and understand their legal rights.</li>\n</ul>\n",
